[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3837856960","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115780#issuecomment-3837856960","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115780","id":3837856960,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kwQzA","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-02T23:44:07Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T23:45:30Z","body":"To be specific, the issue seems to be mipmap LOD bias not working on Vulkan, while it is working on D3D12. Notice how the texture appears much sharper on the second example, even though both are viewed up front (and not from an oblique angle). The *positive* mipmap LOD bias means we are supposed to see a blurrier texture than we normally would.\n\n> Do past versions matter since D3D12 is basically new in 4.6? I can test in previous versions if needed\n\nYes, D3D12 has been around since Godot 4.3 as an option.\n\n@coobenguy Can you upload a minimal reproduction project?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3837856960/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3837937544","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115780#issuecomment-3837937544","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115780","id":3837937544,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kwkeI","user":{"login":"coobenguy","id":76452238,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDUyMjM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76452238?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy","html_url":"https://github.com/coobenguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-03T00:08:08Z","updated_at":"2026-02-03T00:08:08Z","body":"No, unless Im misunderstanding what youre saying, LOD bias seems to work correctly to me. The reason it looks sharp in Vulkan and not D3D12 is BECAUSE anisotropic works correctly in Vulkan and not D3D. When disabling anisotropic filtering with Vulkan, the result is exactly the same as D3D12 with anisotropic  at 16x. Like I say in the report, the only reason I have the bias increased is to make the issue more apparent. \n\nChanging anisotropic quality level has zero observable affect in D3D12.\n\nI figured I wouldnt test on older versions since I recall D3D12 being rewritten for 4.6 but Ive now tested previous versions and added more info to the report and added a mrp\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3837937544/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3838082188","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115780#issuecomment-3838082188","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115780","id":3838082188,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kxHyM","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-03T00:41:40Z","updated_at":"2026-02-03T00:42:58Z","body":"Unable to reproduce on an AMD Radeon RX 6600 using 25.12.1 on either DX12 or Vulkan using 4.6 stable on Windows 11.\n\nTry updating or downgrading your drivers\n\nAlso, try changing the Anisotropic settings when in DX12 to see if things change","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3838082188/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3838246537","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115780#issuecomment-3838246537","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115780","id":3838246537,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kxv6J","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-03T01:17:35Z","updated_at":"2026-02-03T01:20:02Z","body":"I can't reproduce this on 4.6.stable on, Direct3D 12, Vulkan or OpenGL. Changing the anisotropic filter level also works without a restart on D3D12 and Vulkan.\n\n<details open>\n\n<summary>PC specifications</summary>\n\n- **CPU:** AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D\n- **GPU:** NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090 (driver 591.86)\n- **RAM:** 64 GB (2×32 GB DDR5-6000 CL30)\n- **SSD:** Solidigm P44 Pro 2 TB\n- **OS:** Windows 11 24H2\n</details>\n\nDisabled | 16x\n-|-\n<img width=\"1167\" height=\"585\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d74c69bb-3f9c-4d0d-aec5-631be8e9dae3\" /> | <img width=\"1056\" height=\"604\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0cc7e9c3-e286-44b5-805b-11a5f96098f4\" />\n\nMipmap LOD bias works on both D3D12 and Vulkan too.\n\nDouble-check that you aren't globally forcing anisotropic filtering off in the NVIDIA Control Panel or NVIDIA app. In my experience, this setting *can* affect D3D12 apps, at least in certain cases.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3838246537/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3838289700","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115780#issuecomment-3838289700","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115780","id":3838289700,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7kx6ck","user":{"login":"coobenguy","id":76452238,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDUyMjM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76452238?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy","html_url":"https://github.com/coobenguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-03T01:28:37Z","updated_at":"2026-02-03T01:28:37Z","body":"Thank you. Indeed it got switched off in NVIDIA Control Panel at some point. In fact, every setting in the control panel was set to 'off' for whatever reason.... Closing the issue","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3838289700/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]